{"title":"Anti-AI Grifters + College Football Surveillance","link":"https://www.usermag.co/p/anti-ai-grifters-college-football","date":1763332454000,"content":"<h2>The “Anti-AI” Grift</h2><div><figure><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!1sqX!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F5b635fea-9d8b-4636-bf88-1ace2a13bf37_1920x1080.jpeg\"><div><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!1sqX!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F5b635fea-9d8b-4636-bf88-1ace2a13bf37_1920x1080.jpeg\" width=\"561\" height=\"315.5625\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!1sqX!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F5b635fea-9d8b-4636-bf88-1ace2a13bf37_1920x1080.jpeg 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!1sqX!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F5b635fea-9d8b-4636-bf88-1ace2a13bf37_1920x1080.jpeg 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!1sqX!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F5b635fea-9d8b-4636-bf88-1ace2a13bf37_1920x1080.jpeg 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!1sqX!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F5b635fea-9d8b-4636-bf88-1ace2a13bf37_1920x1080.jpeg 1456w\" /><div><div></div></div></div></a><figcaption>Authors of the book <em>If Anyone Builds It, Everyone Dies</em></figcaption></figure></div><p>On Friday, there was a big event in L.A. for <a href=\"https://x.com/willmacaskill/status/1968759901620146427\">a widely-panned</a> book supposedly critiquing the AI industry called <em>If Anyone Builds It, Everyone Dies</em> by Eliezer Yudkowsky and Nate Soare<em>s</em>. I don’t cover the nuances of the AI industry much, but the PR person for the book invited me and I said ‘sure.’ I and a few other tech reporters RSVPd and received confirmation that we’d be attending. A few days later, however, the PR person called and said, actually, I was DISINVITED for being too critical of Silicon Valley. Apparently my reporting on tech billionaires had angered the organizers.</p>\n      <p>\n          <a href=\"https://www.usermag.co/p/anti-ai-grifters-college-football\">\n              Read more\n          </a>\n      </p>","author":"Taylor Lorenz","siteTitle":"usermag.co","siteHash":"95f273abc07d53f60c12a9877d5e701fc5d46103659afbdcd53f0429eec6280d","entryHash":"681f4def7e0ee3b7b3969deee4e520c8dd04fefeb13bf8101b4c426c8474b6ee","category":"Sites"}